  "Area": "Unclassified",
  "Number": 6,
  "Question": "For positive numbers \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) the operation \\(\\spadesuit (x,y)\\) is defined as \\[\\spadesuit (x,y) = x-\\dfrac{1}{y}\\] What is \\(\\spadesuit (2,\\spadesuit (2,2))?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\)",
    "B": "\\(1\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{4}{3}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{5}{3}\\)",
    "E": "\\(2\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Evaluate the inner operation first by substituting into the given rule:\n\\[\n\\spadesuit(2,2)=2-\\frac12=\\frac32.\n\\]\nThis value is positive, so it is an allowed second input for the outer operation. Substituting again gives\n\\[\n\\spadesuit\\left(2,\\frac32\\right)\n=2-\\frac{1}{3/2}\n=2-\\frac23\n=\\boxed{\\frac43}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
